 Adding elements of modern society to the game adds a sense of irony to
the game. Life's a bitch no matter how hard you try to get away from it!
I think this is why Tourists and Doctors were added. They were intended
as jokes, but they are also for the people who like the modern elements.
Nurses, Mad Scientists, Tourists, Doctors, Credit Cards, Keystone Cops,
Pizza, Sinks,... none of these are medieval, but were put in the game for
the humor. They are all important parts of the game though.
 If the game were true to life, the barbarian would not know what to do
with a sink, but the person playing the role has the modern experience to
deal with it.
 I'm not trying to say that the dev team should go out of there way to add
as much modern technology as possible, but that a good (fun) idea should not
be rejected because it has some modern elements.

